<title>USA: South Jersey Hospital System in merger pact - paper.</title>
<headline>South Jersey Hospital System in merger pact - paper.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Jersey Hospital System and Newcomb Health Services Corp plan to announce a merger, the Philadelphia Inquirer reported Wednesday.</p>
<p>The merger, which would take effect Friday, would create the largest health-care provider in Cumberland and Salem Counties, according to the newspaper.</p>
<p>Officials at the hospitals told the newspaper no layoffs were expected, but hundreds of beds could be eliminated in a restructuring over the next several months.</p>
<p>--Steven Dickson, 212-859-1652</p>
